%description:

Tcp.zeroWindowProbe:linux -- the probe of a zero window is an old sequence number without data.

The claim (Tcp.ned): ""linux": a segment without data with SEG.SEQ = SND.UNA - 1, which the
receiver answers with an ACK, as Linux (tcp_xmit_probe_skb())".

The classes: rfc ("rfc", the default), linux ("linux"; LinuxTcp). The code:
TcpConnection::sendProbe(). This test separates "linux" from "rfc".

Host under test: host1, which sends 100000 bytes. Peer: host2, whose application reads nothing.
Observation: level 1, the first segment of host1 after the window closes has no data and the
sequence number one below the acknowledged one.

%# parameter: Tcp.zeroWindowProbe
%# class: linux
%# value: "linux"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.zeroWindowProbe
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"
#include "TcpTestApp.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpZeroWindowProbeLinux")
        .act(action().at(0.0).run<TcpTestApp>("host2.app[0]", [](TcpTestApp& app) {
            app.socket().setAutoRead(false);
            app.socket().bind(1000);
            app.socket().listen();
        }))
        .once(on("host2.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.ackBit == true && tcp.window == 0")
             .capture("una", "tcp.ackNo")
             .describe("the ACK of host2 that closes the window")
             .within(2.0))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == false")
             .first()
                  .assertPacket("pk.dataLength == tcp.headerLength && tcp.sequenceNo == {una} - 1")
             .describe("the probe of host1, without data")
             .within(2.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpZeroWindowProbeLinux compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.zeroWindowProbe = "linux"    # the parameter under test
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
*.host2.app[0].typename = "TcpTestApp"
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpZeroWindowProbeLinux: PASS
